WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:11.640
The North Wind and the Sun were high in the sky.

2
00:00:12.941 --> 00:00:16.324
As usual, the North Wind was bragging to the Sun.

3
00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:20.508
"Watch me blow away these clouds," he said.

4
00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:24.891
"I'm really strong—much stronger than you."

5
00:00:26.953 --> 00:00:29.756
He blew hard and all the clouds scattered.

6
00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:35.279
"See?" the North Wind said with a grin.

7
00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:39.682
"I'm the strongest one in the sky!"

8
00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:42.584
The Sun smiled.

9
00:00:42.604 --> 00:00:46.887
"I'm strong too," she said.

10
00:00:46.907 --> 00:00:50.750
"Ha-ha!" The North Wind laughed loudly.

11
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.892
"You? Strong?

12
00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:57.334
You're always gentle, not strong!"

13
00:00:58.715 --> 00:01:02.558
Just then the Sun spotted a man walking along the road.

14
00:01:03.298 --> 00:01:05.219
The man was wearing a warm coat.

15
00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:09.581
"Let's have a contest," the Sun said.

16
00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:14.784
"The one who makes that man remove his coat is the strongest."

17
00:01:15.985 --> 00:01:20.707
"Sure," the North Wind said, laughing again.

18
00:01:20.727 --> 00:01:24.309
"That will be easy for me.

19
00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:27.331
I'll just blow that coat right off him.

20
00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:29.112
Watch this!"

21
00:01:33.606 --> 00:01:35.347
The North Wind blew hard.

22
00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:40.830
On the road below, dust and leaves flew everywhere.

23
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.051
"Oh!" The man shivered.

24
00:01:44.071 --> 00:01:46.933
"What a chilly wind!"

25
00:01:49.414 --> 00:01:50.275
"That's odd."

26
00:01:51.075 --> 00:01:54.677
The North Wind frowned as the man buttoned up his coat.

27
00:01:56.098 --> 00:01:57.919
"The coat is still on him.

28
00:01:59.119 --> 00:01:59.900
I'll try again."

29
00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:04.317
The North Wind blew again, this time even harder.

30
00:02:08.498 --> 00:02:11.699
But once more, the coat stayed on the man.

31
00:02:11.719 --> 00:02:19.022
"Phew!" By now the North Wind was out of breath and very tired.

32
00:02:19.042 --> 00:02:24.623
"Oh well," the Sun said gently.

33
00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:26.904
"I guess it's my turn."

34
00:02:31.996 --> 00:02:33.798
She moved closer to the man.

35
00:02:33.818 --> 00:02:39.242
"What strange weather," the man said, unbuttoning his coat.

36
00:02:39.262 --> 00:02:41.003
"Now it's lovely out!"

37
00:02:42.224 --> 00:02:44.686
The Sun beamed even more brightly.

38
00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:50.710
It's so warm," the man said.

39
00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.552
"It feels wonderful."

40
00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.553
"Oh no!"

41
00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.836
the North Wind cried as the man removed his coat.

42
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.821
The Sun smiled.

43
00:03:02.841 --> 00:03:06.223
"I guess I won the contest."

44
00:03:06.243 --> 00:03:11.706
"Hmpf!" The North Wind said, taking off.

45
00:03:13.427 --> 00:03:16.309
Below, the man was resting peacefully under a tree.

46
00:03:17.149 --> 00:03:19.390
The Sun kept him warm as he slept.

47
00:03:26.815 --> 00:03:28.936
North Wind," the Sun thought.

48
00:03:29.648 --> 00:03:31.813
"Someday he'll realize something.

49
00:03:32.975 --> 00:03:37.784
It's often better to be gentle than to blow with great strength."
